<title>FRANCE: France to meet Maastricht targets - Arthuis aide.</title>
<headline>France to meet Maastricht targets - Arthuis aide.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chief aide to French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said the government would reach its deficit targets to qualify for European monetary union.</p>
<p>Christian Noyer told an investment seminar luncheon that the &quot;very significant cuts&quot; in budget spending &quot;will permit us to sharply reduce public deficits&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;We have won the battle of stabilising spending in current francs,&quot; Noyer said. This would allow the government to meet the target of reducing France's deficit to three percent of gross domestic product in 1997 to take part in the first wave of membership of a single currency, he said.</p>
</text>
